  "scope": "40 unique pages, indexed 26 January 1690–27 July 1749; original matched passages inspected, earliest first.",
  "conclusion": "One reviewed passage names James Glasgow: the Prosperity of Irvine arrival reported at Greenock on 12 August 1740, published 18 August. The other 39 reviewed pages yielded city or vessel matches. Four Irvine James profiles remain compatible, with no identification proved.",
  "limitations": [
    "This is an initial selected batch, not an exhaustive archive search or proof of the earliest Glasgow surname in print.",
    "The 20 quoted searches used indexed dates 1690–1749 and oldest-first ordering. Only the first page selected from each spelling-variant search was inspected; Glascow captured 20 of 76 result rows.",
    "Search OCR misses long-s and spelling variants. Zero-row captures were not independently validated as exhaustive negative searches.",
    "Dates are Newspapers.com indexed issue dates; two pages contain later printed dates. Source readings were checked against the scans. Exclusions concern the matched passages, not every word of the issues.",
    "Ship homeports and arrival places do not establish the master’s birthplace or residence. Northcopen is retained as printed."
